  "worked_solution": "Since the function is valid starting from $12$ P.M., we can conclude our interval is $[0,4].$\n\nApplying the average value formula, we find that the average value of the function is\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{P}_{\\text{avg}} & =\\frac{1}{b-a}{\\int }_{a}^{b}P(t)\\,\\text{d}t \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4-0}{\\int }_{0}^{4}(200+8\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi }{4}t))\\text{d}t \\\\  & ={\\frac{1}{4}(200t-\\frac{32}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi \\,t}{4}))|}_{0}^{4} \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(200\\cdot 4-\\frac{32}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 4}{4}))-(200\\cdot 0-\\frac{32}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\frac{\\pi \\cdot 0}{4}))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(800-\\frac{32}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(\\pi ))-(-\\frac{32}{\\pi }\\operatorname{cos}\u2061(0))] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[(800-\\frac{32}{\\pi }\\cdot (-1))+\\frac{32}{\\pi }\\cdot 1] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}[800+\\frac{32}{\\pi }+\\frac{32}{\\pi }] \\\\  & =\\frac{1}{4}(800+\\frac{64}{\\pi }) \\\\  & =200+\\frac{16}{\\pi }.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
